WEBVTT

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:04.250
The Intense battle of the newcomers
who bear the burden of Pantasia’s future...

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.310
has finally reached its finale.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:25.000
The champion of the 39th
Pantasia Newcomers’ Battle is...

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:28.240
Azuma Kazuma-kun.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.340
Common sense, huh?

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:36.660
You certainly need knowledge.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.200
But...

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.810
as bakers...

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:41.040
As creators...

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.480
Those of us who have the dreams and the passion

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.760
to be able to overturn common sense are the strongest.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:56.800
And up! And up!

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:57.640
Stop!

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.430
Stop it!

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:00.060
And up! And up!

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:04.960
And this battle has proven the
strength of one who dares to dream.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.440
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.320
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.570
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:16.900
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:22.240
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:25.920
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:43.090
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:51.060
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:58.930
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:06.650
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:14.120
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:23.500
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:32.260
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:36.520
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:39.470
is the light of only you.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.260
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:48.070
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:55.790
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:02:58.130 --> 00:02:59.380
What was that!!

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:01.640
Kawachi, a man’s hard training!

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:06.390
And up! And up!

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:08.420
This is dangerous!
And up! And up!

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.190
Please stop!
And up! And up!

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:14.960
He who is capable of breaking through the
wall of common sense is the strongest, huh?

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.200
It’s my loss then...

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:19.920
Azuma-kun.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:21.860
My loss?

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:22.930
Then, that means...

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:29.220
Stop!

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:33.500
It’s insurance!

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:35.090
In case you lose, of course.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:37.300
And should you betray me,
you know what will happen...

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.610
You understand, right?

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:44.700
I’ve placed a demolition team on standby
at your research facility.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:50.670
Should I transmit a certain
code from this cell phone... Boom!

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.270
Please don’t!

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:55.920
All my research data, second only to
my life in importance, is collected there.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:59.240
Stop!

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:01.180
Goodbye...

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:03.130
to the useless little castle.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:09.120
We’ve received the code to proceed.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:10.540
All personnel evacuate.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:23.360
It’s over.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:26.680
I wonder how you’re feeling...

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:29.930
You embarrassed me, Kanmuri Shigeru.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:32.370
You must feel refreshed after
having lost everything, right?

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:41.200
All my research up until now...

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:44.240
has been reduced to dust.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.780
Shigeru, what’s wrong?

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:01.380
No, it’s just that...

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:04.780
To have thought that I could fulfill my
dream with another’s money and power...

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:09.780
I’m just laughing and laughing at myself for having lived with that naive belief...

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:11.640
Shigeru...

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:12.400
No more!
Shigeru...

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:12.940
No more!

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:19.360
Are you all right, Azuma-san?

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:22.260
No, I’m not!

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:25.130
It hurts...

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:27.640
Congratulations on winning.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.810
Tsukino, I kept our promise, right?

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:42.340
Tsukino...

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:44.900
Thank you, Azuma-san...

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:47.910
At that time...

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:50.350
Azuma-san, it’s all right.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:52.470
It was hard, wasn’t it?

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:54.750
You don’t have to push yourself to fight.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:56.780
It’s all right to run away.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:05:59.250
I’ll protect you.

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:01.780
While I was saying that to you...

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:08.590
I was thinking that I wouldn’t have to watch
your painfully hard matches anymore.

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:10.280
I’m sorry.

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:12.620
I’m ashamed of how weak I am.

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:13.660
But...

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:16.500
thanks to you having fought without running away...

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:18.010
Tsukino...?

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:20.830
It’s the best feeling right now!

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:24.520
I won’t run away from anyone or anything anymore.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:29.550
You really are amazing!

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:31.850
I must do my best, too.

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:34.520
At this rate, the third place match is also...

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:35.540
All right!

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:38.390
With the newcomers’ battle
having finished,

00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:40.600
it’s Night Fever today,
starting this afternoon!

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:41.770
It’s the Fever!

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:42.540
Sounds good!

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:45.550
You can’t call it night if it’s afternoon, can you?

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:46.820
Fever! Fever! Fever! Fever!

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:49.070
I want to go for karaoke as well.
Fever! Fever! Fever! Fever!

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:50.570
I’m hungry!
Fever! Fever! Fever! Fever!

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:53.660
All right! It’s beef steak today
with Azuma’s prize money.

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:55.560
Fever! Fever! Fever!

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:57.060
Just wait one moment!
Fever! Fever! Fever!

00:06:57.620 --> 00:06:59.540
What do you mean it’s over?!

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:02.060
My third place match starts now!

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:03.560
The fever comes after that!

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:05.210
We’re joking.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:06.350
Joking.

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:09.090
I want to go for karaoke quickly.

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:11.430
It’s a joke. A joke.

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:14.100
Hurry up. Hurry up.
We’re going for beef steak.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:16.390
No, we’re serious. Serious!

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:17.270
Hurry up!

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:18.580
Like I said, we’re serious!

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:21.900
They were all serious, weren’t they?

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:23.590
Whatever.

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:26.900
Either way, think of it as if you
were deceived and watch.

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:29.490
The real finale begins now!

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:31.700
I’m going to surprise all of you!

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:32.820
With your hairstyle?

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:34.350
Yeah, it was definitely a surprise.

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:35.510
No!

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:38.140
All right. Listen up.

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:42.460
There’s an extraordinary explanation for this hairstyle.

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:45.210
One week ago,

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:48.700
when I went to the church that
Manager told me about...

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:49.990
What was that?!

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:53.300
So, the Father Graham that Manager told me about

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:55.470
is no more...

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:56.430
Yeah...

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:59.450
He died a peaceful death at age 108 last week.

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:05.240
Matsushiro-san was there at
the funeral, so he should know.

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:12.950
That Afro-Manager. He tricked me!

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:14.820
Making fun of me...

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:15.530
I won’t forgive him!

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:17.410
I’m going home!

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:19.690
You’ve not been tricked.

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:20.020
What?

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:23.290
I’m late with introducing myself.

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:25.880
I’m Sister Mako Graham.

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:28.340
I’m the adopted daughter
of Andrew Graham.

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:31.490
And better at baking French bread than you, at least.

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:34.850
What was that?!

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:37.970
Don’t try to make fun of me.

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:40.140
Unlike Azuma, Kanmuri or Suwabara,

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:43.410
I may not be a genius.

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:48.920
But, I’ve still made it to the third place
match of the Pantasia newcomers’ battle.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:54.200
I couldn’t possibly lose to an amateur like you.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:56.430
Then, let’s have a match.

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:01.290
Sure, whatever.

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:03.580
Like I care if you get embarrassed.

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:05.010
This is really dumb.

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:09.980
Thinking that, I accepted her challenge.

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:35.840
What...?

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:40.850
Wh... What’s with that weird shape?

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:48.350
It’s complete!

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:57.260
So, what do you think of this spectacular bread?!

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:59.140
Compared to this...

00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:00.620
Eat it and see.

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:02.930
This stupid bread...?

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:03.620
Ouch, that hurts!

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:05.520
Fine, fine.

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:06.900
I’ll eat it.

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:09.960
Man...

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:13.000
Exactly what part of this is a French bread.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.330
That complete amateur of a nun.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.530
This... This is...

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:21.710
What the...

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:29.840
It’s a rugged crust, yet...

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:34.570
the insides are perfectly and completely soft.

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:35.440
This is...

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:44.690
The feeling of shouting “Love!” from the core of an afro.

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:47.380
Help me please!

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:51.580
Help me please! Help me please!

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:54.950
Why am I in a bath?

00:10:57.360 --> 00:10:58.340
Maybe...

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:00.800
A-f-ro.

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:03.550
She got me.

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:06.750
This French bread, which looks like an exploded afro,

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:10.560
is much more delicious than my baguette!

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:12.020
In order to prevent the bread

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:15.610
from exploding due to the steam
produced by baking it at high temperatures,

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:18.820
the bread has been slashed more than usual.

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:21.820
Therefore, it doesn’t look
great, but it tastes exceptional.

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:23.320
What was that?!

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:27.130
In the first place,
the shape of French bread...

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:32.460
was selfishly decided 200 years ago by Napoleon.

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:35.840
There is plenty of scope to make different variations.

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:38.720
Is that so...?

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:42.560
So, you lost to a complete
amateur, didn’t you? You shithead!

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:44.300
Shithead?!

00:11:45.020 --> 00:11:48.310
I’ve gone a step lower than a pig, huh?

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:54.810
Let me tell you why you’re a shithead.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:12:00.320
That’s because you’re a
“What was that?!” person.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:01.820
What was that?!

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:04.820
Ah, you said it again,
you annoying little...

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:06.790
I mean, how many times

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:09.830
in your life do you plan on saying “What was that?!”

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:13.580
If you say it about five times
in just one day...

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:14.120
In 365 days, it comes to 1825 times.

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:16.880
What was that
In 365 days, it comes to 1825 times.

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.590
If you live for 50 more years,
it comes to 91,250 times!
What was that

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:22.510
If you live for 50 more years,
it comes to 91,250 times!

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:24.840
It makes me want to say “What was that?!”

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:25.930
What was that?!

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:26.600
Oh shit.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:28.270
Listen up.

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:31.060
Putting “What was that?!” into words shows that

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:33.100
you’re surprised by others.

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:36.440
An-pan, melon-bread, uguisu-pan.
Uguisu pan (<b>鶯 ぱん), or nightingale bread is the affectionate name given to a bread roll with green bean jam filling.</b>

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:38.490
With bold creations not bound by common sense,

00:12:38.490 --> 00:12:41.360
the truly outstanding bakers reaped success by

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:45.610
surprising others rather than
getting surprised themselves.

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:48.580
But, in your case it’s always “What was that?!”

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:51.170
You’re on the side of being surprised.

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:55.120
You’re not even a graduate from Harvard

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:57.590
and yet you show off that
half-assed knowledge of yours.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:00.300
You are bound by common sense

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:02.590
and are always surprised by the geniuses in the end.

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:07.050
You’re just a side character shouting “What was that?!”

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:11.010
That is your true nature.

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:13.100
What was that?!

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:16.610
What was that?! What was that?!

00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:30.360
A side character, huh?

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:31.990
That was harsh.

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:34.450
But... that may be true.

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:37.710
I... What can I do?

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:42.720
As long as you are shackled by common sense, you cannot win against the geniuses.

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:47.250
I suggest starting with outward appearances,
that is, with how you present yourself.

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:47.720
What?

00:13:48.380 --> 00:13:49.880
When serving the Lord,

00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:52.930
a large number of people shave themselves bald.

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:56.560
So, if you’re to become a bold man who has
cast away the shackles of common sense...

00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:58.270
it has to be an afro.

00:13:58.270 --> 00:14:00.980
Right? Don’t you think so?

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:02.480
I don’t.

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:04.100
Well, you must.

00:14:04.100 --> 00:14:07.360
Throw away common sense. Get yourself an afro.

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:11.440
Actually, in the past, Matsushiro-san

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:15.280
also had an inferiority complex against
geniuses like Kirisaki-san and Mokoyama-san.

00:14:15.280 --> 00:14:17.490
He says he was a
“What did you say?!” person.

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:18.700
What did you say?!

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:21.460
What did you say?! What did you say?!

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:24.620
But, once he got his afro,

00:14:24.620 --> 00:14:26.670
he escaped from the shell of common sense.

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:30.100
With his now bold heart and body,
he developed new creations...

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:39.020
and became Japan’s #1 French bread baker.

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:42.440
What was that?!

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:46.940
Throw away your common sense and get an afro!

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:50.660
If you do that, a new path will unfold for sure.

00:14:51.190 --> 00:14:52.900
Come, come, come, come, come!

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:54.160
To become a man, it just has to be an afro!

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:55.740
Man
To become a man, it just has to be an afro!

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:55.750
To become a man, it just has to be an afro!

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:58.070
Those who believe will be saved.

00:14:58.070 --> 00:14:59.950
And now, that has to be you.

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:02.830
Come... Come, come, come, come, come, come!

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:05.800
I get the feeling that if I believe,
I really never will be able to go back.

00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:13.800
I’ll become a man as well!

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:19.520
And thus began my intense afro
training at St. Andrew’s Church.

00:15:20.260 --> 00:15:24.610
The path was fearsome
enough to flay away your body hair.

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:33.030
This anime is really good.

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:35.900
I really hate this anime.

00:15:35.900 --> 00:15:37.410
What was that?!

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:41.380
Hey! It’s terrible. Terrible!

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:43.250
Look at this.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:44.750
UFO’s have been sighted!

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:46.090
What was that?!

00:15:53.630 --> 00:15:54.670
Hello.

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:55.760
I’m Afro-kun.

00:15:56.170 --> 00:15:57.380
What was that?!

00:15:57.380 --> 00:15:59.390
One afro coming up!

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:03.150
Not even my father ever hit me.

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:05.100
I can’t do this anymore.

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:06.150
This training...

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:11.020
You saw, didn’t you?

00:16:11.020 --> 00:16:12.740
What was that?!

00:16:19.110 --> 00:16:20.200
And, with that...

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:21.950
I was granted the afro.

00:16:21.950 --> 00:16:26.750
And I’ve trained to create things that are
bold and not shackled by common sense.

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:29.330
Listen up people!

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:33.000
“What was *beep*?!!” no longer exists in my dictionary.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:34.760
I’ll never say it again!

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:36.510
Well done, Kawachi!

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:41.930
To not be shackled by common sense, huh?

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:44.640
I can bring myself to comprehend the objective, but...

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:45.730
I’m worried.

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:48.230
You’ve got a great afro there.

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:51.700
But, Kawachi.

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:56.240
I’m sorry to tell you that
the nun you met is...

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:00.000
A FAKE!

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:05.500
You were taken for a royal ride.

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:07.340
What was that?!

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:11.090
You...

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:13.180
big fool!

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:24.510
Kawachi!

00:17:24.510 --> 00:17:27.400
For what reason did you get an afro?

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:31.480
If should have been to have attained
a heart that doesn’t waver at anything,

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:33.980
and to create things that are bold...

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:35.520
and not shackled by common sense!

00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:37.150
And yet...

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:39.360
you were fooled by a simple lie like that,

00:17:39.360 --> 00:17:41.520
and were surprised into a “What was that?!”

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:46.000
You think you can win against that man at this rate?

00:17:47.490 --> 00:17:49.500
That’s true, Manager.

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:51.170
It’s just as you say.

00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:53.670
But...

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:58.420
Isn’t it just as bad if I’m unable to even move
after receiving that strong a punch?

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:01.130
Isn’t that the real problem right now?

00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:03.230
You trying to make me forfeit?

00:18:04.010 --> 00:18:06.100
Kawachi, I’m disappointed in you.

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:07.820
Changing your hairstyle into
something stupid like that...

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:10.810
I didn’t know who it was in the beginning.

00:18:11.430 --> 00:18:13.520
Did you think that you’d get stronger

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:15.320
by making your hairstyle the same as your teacher’s?

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:18.650
I won’t be defeated by such a bluff.

00:18:18.650 --> 00:18:20.820
I wonder...

00:18:21.360 --> 00:18:25.830
It’s true that this hairstyle may appear like a bluff.

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:27.120
But...

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:30.330
what I learned in the past week is no bluff!

00:18:30.950 --> 00:18:32.540
I’ll show it to you.

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:34.840
My... My...

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:37.340
Singing French Bread!

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:45.470
Suwabara, you’re surprised, right?

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:46.560
Your...

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:49.100
What did you say?!

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:52.390
I can just see you panicking.

00:18:52.390 --> 00:18:53.640
Hey, Kawachi.

00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:55.100
Kawachi!

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:57.560
Suwabara’s already gone.

00:18:57.560 --> 00:18:59.780
The match looks like it’s about to start.

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:03.370
What was that?!

00:19:03.860 --> 00:19:05.110
Starting now,

00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:09.370
the 39th Pantasia Newcomers’ Battle
third place match will begin!

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:11.880
I’m really sorry.

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:14.330
Suwabara Kai.

00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:15.500
Kawachi Kyousuke.

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:16.880
Combatants, step forward.

00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:21.390
I’m worried.

00:19:22.090 --> 00:19:22.890
Begin!

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:29.390
I’ll show you, Suwabara.

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:33.400
What I’ve learned.

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:49.290
What... I learned at that church.

00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:53.920
That’s...

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:55.040
Are those chopsticks?

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:55.910
It’s chopsticks.

00:19:55.910 --> 00:19:58.420
He’s stabbed his chopsticks into the bread.

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:02.300
If the bread were rice,

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:04.640
that would be something that he’d be punished for.

00:20:06.880 --> 00:20:11.890
The shape of French bread was
decided by Napoleon 200 years ago.

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:14.390
I learned that there were no rules to it originally.

00:20:14.390 --> 00:20:16.400
It’s the same with the number
of slashes across the bread.

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:21.110
Originally, the slashes were added
in order to allow for the expansion

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:25.190
of the bread by allowing steam inside
to escape when the bread was baked.

00:20:25.190 --> 00:20:28.370
The shape of the slashes doesn’t matter.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:31.420
Most importantly,
my Singing French Bread...

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:34.950
can’t even be baked
with just the traditional

00:20:34.950 --> 00:20:36.920
number or shape of slashes.

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:39.920
The guy with the bandanna is
doing something amazing as well.

00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:44.300
It looks like the chatter over
Suwabara’s bread is increasing as well.

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:48.300
Well, I didn’t think he’d be that easy to defeat either.

00:20:49.050 --> 00:20:50.010
But...

00:20:50.010 --> 00:20:53.310
this is not like some 1296 layer croissant.

00:20:55.060 --> 00:20:56.140
That shape is...

00:20:56.140 --> 00:20:58.230
A... A French bread!

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:00.280
He’s making French bread as well?!

00:21:00.850 --> 00:21:03.280
But... there’s nothing to get surprised over...

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:10.790
Lo... Long!

00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:12.950
Kawachi!

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:15.290
It appears you’re making French bread as well.

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:19.870
But, in that case, you absolutely can’t win!

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:27.010
Originally developed as a lethal
weapon to use in the finals...

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:29.050
My ultimate French bread.

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:31.480
You can’t win against my Dancing French Bread!!

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:34.770
What was that?!

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:39.310
Ouch!

00:21:39.310 --> 00:21:40.820
Who was that?

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:45.030
I shouldn’t. I shouldn’t.

00:21:45.770 --> 00:21:48.030
That’s right.
I shouldn’t be saying “What was that?!”

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:50.490
It’s just as Manager and the Sister say.

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:54.530
There’s no way that someone who’s constantly afraid

00:21:54.530 --> 00:21:56.960
of his opponent can win.

00:21:57.490 --> 00:21:59.290
Right now, I have an afro.

00:21:59.960 --> 00:22:02.460
I won’t lose so easily.

00:22:02.830 --> 00:22:05.970
Believe in yourself, Kawachi Kyousuke.

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:08.800
Listen up, Suwabara.

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:12.760
While your French bread may dance,
my French bread can sing!

00:22:15.470 --> 00:22:16.600
Huh?

00:22:17.760 --> 00:22:19.470
I’m looking forward to that, Kawachi.

00:22:20.850 --> 00:22:23.480
But, Suwabara has already begun baking his bread.

00:22:24.730 --> 00:22:26.990
What was that?!

00:22:29.070 --> 00:22:30.070
It’s no use, is it?

00:22:30.070 --> 00:22:31.320
It’s no use.

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:33.040
Yeah, it’s no use.

00:22:54.480 --> 00:22:56.240
On this chest, big and strong

00:22:56.240 --> 00:22:58.360
A look that glitters and doesn't lose.

00:22:58.360 --> 00:23:00.360
That's what I searched for, fumbling in the wind.

00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:01.660
The answer for now is...

00:23:01.660 --> 00:23:04.580
For now, I'll watch the situation and wait for a chance.
I got the patience to wait at a distance.

00:23:04.580 --> 00:23:06.370
A prisoner who just screams is no good.

00:23:06.370 --> 00:23:08.160
Just Follow Me! I'll lend you my shoulder occasionally.

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:18.260
It's by no means a fleeting dream.

00:23:18.260 --> 00:23:21.140
Let this sentiment reach you. Heart to Heart, Soul to Soul.

00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:23.180
The seasons turn. Splendid as a spring storm.

00:23:23.180 --> 00:23:24.590
Win Big is the motto.

00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:29.390
Does a thing like eternity really exist?

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:31.230
And so we... C'mon.

00:23:32.610 --> 00:23:36.780
Yeah, yeah, we live to touch the one shining moment.

00:23:53.710 --> 00:23:57.590
To all the soldiers fighting today using the tail wind...

00:24:05.540 --> 00:24:07.050
My Singing French Bread is going to win!

00:24:07.050 --> 00:24:09.000
My Dancing French Bread is going to win!

00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:09.800
It’s going to sing!

00:24:09.800 --> 00:24:10.510
It’s going to dance!

00:24:10.510 --> 00:24:12.750
Oh, then we have a musical next time?

00:24:14.640 --> 00:24:15.630
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:15.630 --> 00:24:17.340
The last match of the Newcomers’ Battle!!

00:24:17.340 --> 00:24:18.930
The Singing and Dancing French Breads!

00:24:18.930 --> 00:24:19.970
Be sure to watch!

00:24:20.350 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.140 --> 00:24:25.230
Water from the bread evaporates through the slashes,

00:24:25.230 --> 00:24:25.270
A light and fluffy French bread
Water from the bread evaporates through the slashes,

00:24:25.270 --> 00:24:27.970
giving rise to a light and fluffy French bread.
A light and fluffy French bread

00:24:27.970 --> 00:24:29.150
The area between two slashes is called a “bloom.”

00:24:29.150 --> 00:24:31.740
The browned edges of the bread is called an “ear.”

00:24:32.020 --> 00:24:34.450
Really?!
